    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ancient Native American habitation dates back millennia in the area that is now Forest, Louisiana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/forest_louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Poverty Point site near Epps, within West Carroll Parish, is one of North America’s oldest complex hunter‑gatherer settlements, built between 1700 and 1100 BCE.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/forest_louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the late 19th century, railroads linked Forest to larger markets, shifting commerce from river steamboats to rail transport of cotton and timber.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/forest_louisiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Steamboats on Bayou Macon in the 1830s carried cotton to Mississippi River ports, sparking growth of trading posts and villages like Forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/forest_louisiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Forest was officially incorporated as a village in 1966 under Louisiana’s Lawrason Act, marking its transition from an unincorporated community to a municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/forest_louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The village’s economy today relies on agriculture, with cotton, soybeans, and corn as major crops, alongside forestry and related industries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
